Title: Nadi
Credit: Written by
Author: Sample fixture (indian-regional profile; defects injected on purpose)
Contact: fixture@example.com

FADE IN:

EXT. GODAVARI BANK - DAWN

Mist off the water. Coracles nose the shallows. RAJU (30s), boatman,
bails his coracle with a cut-open can.

RAJU
Ammaki cheppu, nenu vastanu.

SAROJA (50s) watches from the steps with a brass pot on her hip.

SAROJA
You said that last week also.

RAJU
Last week the river was low.

INT. SAROJA'S HOUSE - MORNING

Smoke from the stove. Saroja grinds chilli. Raju eats standing up.

SAROJA
The panchayat meets today.

RAJU
Let them meet.

SAROJA
They will take the landing.

RAJU
Then I will take it back.

EXT. GODAVARI BANK - DAY

A song sequence begins here as Raju rows downriver and the villagers
dance along the bank in three costume changes.

EXT. PANCHAYAT GROUND - DAY

Plastic chairs in rows. RAJU stands. The SARPANCH (60s) does not.

SARPANCH
The landing is village property.

RAJU
The landing is my father's.

రాజు
Naa nanna kattinadi.

SARPANCH
Bring the paper.

EXT. GODAVARI BANK - NIGHT

Raju sits alone in the coracle with a lantern. The water takes the
light and gives none of it back.

SAROJA
(from the steps)
Come up. It's late.

RAJU
Not yet.

EXT. GODAVARI BANK - DAWN

The landing has a chain across it. Raju cuts it with a hacksaw and
pushes the coracle out.

FADE OUT.
